Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:49:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 413/488] Structured output: the grammar bitmask as a TileLang
 kernel

The V2 runner's grammar bitmask was a Triton kernel; the TileLang one
keeps its grid (a block a mask row and 8192 tokens), masks the same
tokens and marks the same rejected draft inputs, bit for bit. The
block's bitmask words go through shared memory so each thread's stores
coalesce. The Triton kernel stays as the test's reference.
